        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to other users' accounts or to any part of the service</li>
        <li>Interfere with or disrupt the service's infrastructure or other users' enjoyment of the service</li>
        <li>Use automated scripts or bots to access the service without prior written consent</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="user-content">3. User Content and Licensing</h2>
      <p>You retain full ownership of all content you create and publish on fanfiction.fyi, including stories, chapters, comments, and other works.</p>
      <p>By publishing content on fanfiction.fyi, you grant us a <strong>non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free</strong> license to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Host, store, display, and reproduce your content as necessary to provide the service</li>
        <li>Distribute your content to other users according to the visibility and access settings you configure</li>
        <li>Create ephemeral copies as required for caching, backup, and performance optimization</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This license persists for as long as your content remains on the service. You may remove your content at any time, at which point this license will terminate — except for cached or backup copies, which will be purged in due course.</p>

      <h2 id="content-guidelines">4. Content Guidelines</h2>
      <p>You are solely responsible for the content you publish. By posting content on fanfiction.fyi, you represent and warrant that:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your content does not violate any applicable law</li>
        <li>You have the right to publish the content, and it does not infringe upon the copyrights, trademarks, or other intellectual property rights of any third party</li>
        <li>Your content does not contain malware, spam, or other harmful material</li>
        <li>Your content complies with all applicable content-rating and labeling requirements</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We reserve the right to remove any content that violates these guidelines or that we reasonably believe is harmful to the community, without prior notice.</p>

      <h2 id="disclaimer">5. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
      <p>fanfiction.fyi is provided on an <strong>"AS IS"</strong> and <strong>"AS AVAILABLE"</strong> basis. To the fullest extent permitted by law, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including but not limited to implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.</p>
      <p>We do not warrant that the service will be uninterrupted, secure, or error-free. We are not responsible for the content, accuracy, or opinions of any user-published content.</p>

      <h2 id="limitation-liability">6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, fanfiction.fyi and its operators shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, including but not limited to loss of data, loss of profits, or loss of goodwill, arising out of or in connection with your use of the service — even if we have been advised of the possibility of such damages.</p>
